## 3. Conclusion and Possible Changes

Overall, my research shows that automatic window systems can be designed in several different ways depending on their purpose and complexity. Some systems focus on detecting rain, while others focus on temperature, humidity, or air quality. My project focuses on using temperature and light to control a window automatically.
I do not plan to completely change my design because the current components should be enough to demonstrate the main idea. However, I may need to improve the sensor wiring and adjust the code so the servo responds reliably. I could also consider adding a limit switch in the future to prevent the servo mechanism from moving beyond its intended range.
My next goal is to get consistent readings from both sensors, combine them into one working program, and demonstrate the automatic window movement.
